==============================================================================
move_joint_measure.py -- joint test of AKR 9.1's apex-only move
exact Fraction arithmetic throughout; no floats
==============================================================================

SELF-TESTS ON THE PRIMITIVES
  [PASS] orientR ccw > 0
  [PASS] orientR cw  < 0
  [PASS] orientR collinear = 0
  [PASS] orientR matches the Lean formula on a sample
  [PASS] on_closed at start endpoint
  [PASS] on_closed at end endpoint
  [PASS] on_closed at interior point
  [PASS] on_closed rejects the collinear extension
  [PASS] on_closed rejects an off-line point
  [PASS] proper_cross on a genuine X
  [PASS] proper_cross FALSE at a shared endpoint (touching, not crossing)
  [PASS] proper_cross FALSE for a T-touch
  [PASS] SimpleClosed accepts a convex heptagon
  [PASS] SimpleClosed ACCEPTS three collinear vertices (deliberate)
  [PASS] SimpleClosed REJECTS a self-crossing heptagon
  [PASS] SimpleClosed REJECTS an adjacent-side backtrack (conjunct 3)
  [PASS] SimpleClosed REJECTS a repeated vertex (conjunct 1)
  [PASS] moveV changes exactly one vertex
  [PASS] moveV moves it by exactly e*E
  [PASS] moveV with e=0 is the identity
  [PASS] test square-ish P is simple
  [PASS] coincSet finds the translate's shared vertices
  [PASS] designed X-pair: both simple
  [PASS] designed X-pair: exactly one coincidence
  [PASS] a coincidence puts 2 entries in segDeg and 2 in segDegP
  [PASS] finite_intersection says NO on an overlapping collinear pair
  [PASS] finite_intersection says YES on a transversal pair
  all self-tests passed

direction grid : 80 primitive integer directions, |dx|,|dy| <= 5
e grid         : ['1/1000', '-1/1000', '1/100', '-1/100', '1/10', '-1/10', '1/4', '-1/4', '1/2', '-1/2', '1', '-1', '2', '-2', '4', '-4']
scan size      : 1280 (E,e) pairs per instance

designed D1 transversal-X: simpleP=True simpleQ=True finite=True coincSet=[(0, 0)]
designed D2 non-crossing-wedges: simpleP=True simpleQ=True finite=True coincSet=[(0, 0)]
designed D3 collinear-apex-X: simpleP=True simpleQ=True finite=True coincSet=[(1, 1)]

INSTANCE GENERATION
  random polygon pairs drawn                     : 84
  (i,j) coincidence candidates examined          : 2471
    discarded: infinite intersection after gluing: 252
  instances kept, by kind:
    plain  (coincidence only)                    : 60
    hardP  (Q-vertex on a P-side at the apex,
            i.e. a segDeg entry the move destroys): 55
    hardN  (a FROZEN neighbour incidence P[i+-1]
            on a Q-side)                         : 40
    hardM  (two or more coincidences)            : 20
    designed adversarial                         : 3
  TOTAL instances                                : 178

  STRUCTURAL CHECK: 'apex also on a further Q-side' occurrences  : 0
    That kind was requested but is impossible: P[i] = Q[j], so such
    an incidence would be Q touching its own boundary, which
    SimpleClosed forbids.  Every coincidence therefore carries
    exactly 2 segDeg + 2 segDegP entries -- a fixed debt of 4.

  LOCAL BUDGET AT THE APEX (max local crossings creatable, by the
  cone criterion -- must be >= 4 to pay the debt of 4):
    max local crossings = 1 : 22 instances
    max local crossings = 2 : 97 instances
    max local crossings = 3 : 33 instances
    max local crossings = 4 : 26 instances

