==============================================================================
THE MECHANISM: the debt is 4, the local budget is the cone count
==============================================================================
  A coincidence P[i]=Q[j] contributes exactly 4 entries to MEASURE
  (segDeg (i-1,j),(i,j) and segDegP (j-1,i),(j,i)); the move destroys
  all four.  The only local repayment is new crossings between the two
  moved P-sides and the two Q-sides at the apex, which the cone
  criterion caps at `max local crossings`.

   max local crossings |    n  small-e dM>0   dM=0   dM<0   none
                     1 |   22             1      1     20      0
                     2 |   97             1      4     92      0
                     3 |   33             3      4     26      0
                     4 |   26             6     20      0      0

